Project:      idevicerestore
Upstream:     https://github.com/libimobiledevice/idevicerestore
Base commit:  540c352c4c44896f7415abef87a166e8bbaea9b0
Licence:      LGPL-2.1-or-later per the source-file headers; the repository's COPYING/README carry the LGPL-3.0 text. This patch is offered under the same terms as the files it modifies.
Description:
  Adds src/t1.c + src/t1.h and hooks them into idevicerestore.c and restore.c: opt-in Apple T1 / iBridge1,1
  (x619ap) EmbeddedOS restore support. Every hook is a no-op unless an IDEVICERESTORE_T1_* environment
  variable is set, so an unpatched-style run behaves exactly like upstream. What it adds:
  - Firmware-bundle compatibility: Apple's iBridge1_1Customer.bundle has no SupportedProductTypes, which
    upstream rejects; in T1 mode a BuildIdentity must instead match the device's ApChipID/ApBoardID.
  - No OS filesystem: an EmbeddedOS restore ships OSRamdisk instead of an OS component, so the OS
    path lookup/extraction is skipped.
  - StartRestore options for EmbeddedOS (ApBootstrapOnly=0, PersonalizedDuringPreflight=1, FlashNOR=1,
    SystemImage/ShouldRestoreSystemImage/RootToInstall/UpdateBaseband=0, optional
    CreateFilesystemPartitions, FDRMemoryStorePath, RestoreBootArgs override) and a keys-only log
    of the options sent.
  - FDR memory store round-trip: advertises FDRMemoryCommit in SupportedDataTypes when FDR output is
    armed, saves the committed store to a 0600 file and acknowledges the commit (pass A); replays a
    saved store as FDRMemoryStoreData inside the RootTicket message (pass B); optional FDRTrustData
    key in the trust-data reply.
  - Preflight capture: the personalized combined memboot (OSRamdisk||KernelCache||DeviceTree||SEP,
    bare concatenation) and the ApImg4Ticket from the SAME TSS response, written 0600.
  - Phase 14: a mode that performs no restore; it replays that image+ticket pair to a T1 in recovery
    (auto-boot=false, send ticket, upload image, setenv boot-args, blind memboot with bRequest=1).
  Nothing identity-bearing is logged: only sizes and key names.
